title: a frontmatter value ending in --- corrupts the task and bricks the whole board
updated: 2026-08-09T17:00:27Z
---

Verified twice, independently. One ordinary user input makes the whole board
unusable with no way back through karr.

## Mechanism

`lib/App/karr/Task.pm:141`:

    my ($yaml, $body) = $content =~ m{\A---\n(.+?)---(?:\n(.*))?\z}s

The closing `---` is **not anchored to a line start**. `Dump` writes a value
like `title: Release v1 ---` unquoted, and the non-greedy `(.+?)` then cuts the
frontmatter in the middle of that line.

kanban-md does not have this bug: `splitFrontmatter`
(`../kanban-md/internal/task/file.go:63`) looks for the literal `"\n---\n"`.

## Reproduction — board bricked by a block reason

    karr create "Normal task" --body hello
    karr edit 1 --block "waiting ---"      -> "Updated task 1"  exit 0
    karr list    -> Missing required arguments: id, title at Git.pm line 471   exit 1
    karr board   -> same
    karr show 1  -> same
    karr delete 1 --yes -> same

`blocked` is dumped first alphabetically, so it takes the whole frontmatter with
it. **Even `delete` cannot save you** — it loads the task before deleting. The
only way out is a raw `git update-ref -d`.

## Reproduction — silent data corruption

    karr create "Release v1 ---" --body "important notes"
    karr show 1
      -> Task #1: Release v1                   # title truncated
      -> Body:  updated: 2026-08-09T15:30:39Z  # rest of the frontmatter is now body
                ---
                important notes

Any frontmatter string value triggers it: `--title`, `--tags "rel---"`,
`--assignee`, `--estimate`, `--due`.

## Fix

Anchor the closing delimiter to a line start (`^---$` with `/m`, or split on
`\n---\n` the way kanban-md does). Regression test must cover a value ending in
`---` in title, tags and block reason, and must assert the board still lists.

Consider also: writing frontmatter values quoted would make this unreachable
from the write side, but the parser must be fixed regardless — karr has to be
able to read what an editor or kanban-md wrote.
